The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (cifs_sb->root) {
    // Release cached dentries
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because `cifs_kill_sb` releases cached dentries regardless of whether the filesystem mount was successful or not. If the mount failed and `cifs_sb->root` is not populated, then the function attempts to dereference and release resources that are not valid or properly initialized.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (cifs_sb->root) {
    node = rb_first(root);
    // Release cached dentries
    dput(cifs_sb->root);
    cifs_sb->root = NULL;
}
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that the release of cached dentries only happens if `cifs_sb->root` is populated, indicating that the filesystem mount is complete. This prevents the invalid dereferencing of pointers and ensures that only valid resources are being managed.

